The invention relates to a method for producing and/or capturing neutrons, comprising the following steps:

a) exposing nuclei selected from protons, deuterons, and/or tritons to an electric field to extract the nuclei and direct the extracted nuclei toward a target (20) containing free electrons;

b) optionally, exposing the nuclei to a spatial and/or temporal gradient of a first magnetic field to impart a predefined orientation to the magnetic moments of the nuclei;

c) either exposing the target to a second magnetic field to impart a predefined orientation to the magnetic moments of the target’s free electrons;

d) or using an electron-donating superparamagnetic material such that the electrons in the free layers of the material are oriented along preferred directions determined by the orientation of the resulting magnetic moment of the superparamagnetic material; and

e) optionally, when a superparamagnetic material is used, refraining from exposing the proton beam and/or the target to external magnetic fields.

A heating device and/or a magnetic-field-generating device may be required to activate the material’s superparamagnetic properties.
